<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Cyzicus</h1><p class="st-meta">675 BCE – 25 CE (approx.) · capital Cyzicus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Milesian colony on the Sea of Marmara whose electrum coins circulated across the Greek world and which withstood Mithridates in 73 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cyzicus was founded by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/miletus">Miletus</a> on the isthmus of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapidag-peninsula">Arctonnesus</a> peninsula, on the southern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Propontis</a>; the register follows the date c. 675 BCE, while an earlier foundation c. 756 BCE is also recorded. Its two harbours made it a natural stopping point on the route to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From the 6th century BCE Cyzicus issued electrum staters, the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyzicene">Cyzicenes</a>', widely used in trade. It was ruled by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and paid tribute in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a>. In 410 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcibiades">Alcibiades</a> destroyed a Spartan fleet off the city. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> Cyzicus was a close ally of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-pergamon">Kingdom of Pergamon</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Cyzicus withstood a long siege by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates</a> in 73 BCE until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-licinius-lucullus">Lucullus</a> relieved it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> rewarded it as a free city. It lost that status in 20 BCE, regained it, and lost it finally under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> in 25 CE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cyzicus.jpg" alt="Cyzicus" width="320" height="243"><figcaption>Image: G.dallorto · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istanbul_-_Museo_archeol._-_Auriga_greco_-_Arcaico,_sec._VI_aC,_da_Cizico_-_Foto_G._Dall%27Orto_28-5-2006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>675 BCE – 25 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cyzicus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion; cult of Kore</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ionic Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kyzikos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-325&amp;focus=cyzicus" aria-label="Cyzicus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5365 734 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cyzicus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5685 990L6140 1251M5685 990L5591 1068M5685 990L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M5591 1068h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5685 990h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5685 990h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-325&amp;focus=cyzicus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

